### Docker & Infrastructure

#### [NEW] [docker-compose.yml](file:///Users/taranjain/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/healthcare-platform/docker-compose.yml)
- PostgreSQL 15 container on port **5432** (`POSTGRES_USER=healthcare`, `POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<generated>`, `POSTGRES_DB=healthcare_db`)
- Redis 7 container on port **6379**
- Backend container on port **4000** (depends on postgres, redis)
- Frontend container on port **3000** (depends on backend)
- Named volumes for `pg_data`, `redis_data`, `uploads`

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **PostgreSQL Connection Details** (inside Docker network):
> - **Host**: `postgres` (service name) or `localhost:5432` from host
> - **User**: `healthcare`
> - **Password**: Set via `.env` file (auto-generated on first run)
> - **Database**: `healthcare_db`
> - **Connection URL**: `postgresql://healthcare:<password>@postgres:5432/healthcare_db`

#### [NEW] [.env.example](file:///Users/taranjain/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/healthcare-platform/.env.example)
- All environment variables with placeholder values
- Instructions to generate secrets

